            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Background Atopic dermatitis, also known as atopic eczema, is a chronic inflammatory disorder of the skin characterised by acute exacerbations of skin dryness, rash and pruritus. It is often associated with allergic disorders such as asthma, food allergies and rhinitis.</AbstractText>
